                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I sometimes delve into Hidden Object Adventure Games because they're a fun palette cleanser for when i've grown frustrated by one of the larger RPG/Adventure titles i'm playing and I need a quick win.  4hrs is a relatively quick win.   \nThere's a decent plot here surrounding the little \"Find X for Y\" dynamic every Hidden Object Game has which surrounds a Parallel World.  Helsing Narrative too so it ties in with Dracula/Demon Hunters.\n\nHonestly I was getting vibes that tied back to the old Ravenloft Games.   Beautiful Soundtrack, Beautiful Artwork.  Nothing really felt Ai-Vibey.   Definitely worth peoples time.",
